From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] media: gc2145: do not log the expected probe-time i2c failure

Every boot logs three of these:

  gc2145 3-003c: gc2145_write_regs: error -6: addr=fe, data=00

which looks like the sensor is broken. It is not. The sequence is:

  gc2145_probe -> gc2145_identify -> gc2145_read16(GC2145_REG_CHIP_ID)
               -> gc2145_switch_bank(0xf0): current_bank is 0xff after
                  gc2145_power_on, so bank 0 has to be selected first
               -> gc2145_write_regs(GC2145_REG_RESET /* 0xfe */, 0x00)
               -> NAK, -ENXIO

and probe already knows this happens - it is what the comment next to the
identify call describes, "The camera is not reachable this early during boot
on some boards", and it answers with -EPROBE_DEFER. The three messages are
three deferred attempts; the fourth succeeds and the camera works.

So the transfer failing is expected here, and only here. Log it at debug
level while identifying and leave the error path alone everywhere else,
where a NAK really does mean something went wrong.

Upstream-Status: Pending

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/gc2145.c
@@ -486,6 +486,12 @@
 	bool flips_grabbed;
 	/* a fixed-value test pattern must not be metered, see s_ctrl */
 	bool test_pattern_holds_aec;
+	/*
+	 * Probing the chip id is allowed to fail: the sensor is not always
+	 * reachable that early during boot, and probe just defers. Do not
+	 * shout about the i2c transfers it makes while that is expected.
+	 */
+	bool identifying;
 
 	u8 current_bank;
 
@@ -528,9 +534,14 @@
 
 	ret = i2c_transfer(client->adapter, &msg, 1);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		v4l2_err(&sensor->sd,
-			 "%s: error %d: addr=%x, data=%*ph\n",
-			 __func__, ret, (u32)addr, data_size, data);
+		if (sensor->identifying)
+			dev_dbg(&client->dev,
+				"%s: error %d: addr=%x, data=%*ph\n",
+				__func__, ret, (u32)addr, data_size, data);
+		else
+			v4l2_err(&sensor->sd,
+				 "%s: error %d: addr=%x, data=%*ph\n",
+				 __func__, ret, (u32)addr, data_size, data);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
@@ -556,9 +567,13 @@
 
 	ret = i2c_transfer(client->adapter, msg, 2);
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		v4l2_err(&sensor->sd,
-			 "%s: error %d: start_index=%x, data_size=%d\n",
-			 __func__, ret, (u32)addr, data_size);
+		if (sensor->identifying)
+			dev_dbg(&client->dev, "%s: read error %d\n",
+				__func__, ret);
+		else
+			v4l2_err(&sensor->sd,
+				 "%s: error %d: start_index=%x, data_size=%d\n",
+				 __func__, ret, (u32)addr, data_size);
 		return ret;
 	}
 
@@ -3238,7 +3253,9 @@
 	if (ret)
 		goto entity_cleanup;
 
+	sensor->identifying = true;
 	ret = gc2145_identify(sensor);
+	sensor->identifying = false;
 	if (ret) {
 		/*
 		 * The camera is not reachable this early during boot on
